.env*

# ...and the same files when the leading dot is missing. `.env*` does not match
# `env.local`, so a file saved without the dot carries the service role key and
# the admin password straight into `git add .` without a word of complaint.
# Happened on 31-08; caught before any commit, hence these three lines.
env*.local
env.example
env.demo

# Client e-mail exports (.eml). These are correspondence with CDNA and Axon, not
# project source, and they do not belong on GitHub even in a private repo. They
# were committed once and stripped from the branch history on 31-08; this rule
# is what stops them coming back. Read them locally — see the project memory.
docs/emails/

# temp artifacts (dev server log + prod vercel-link backup)
.dev-server.log
.vercel.prod-backup/
.gstack/
